{"year":"2025","content":[{"type":"text","content_text":"The 30th edition was scheduled for January 12, 2025, but was postponed twice because of the Southern California wildfires and took place on February 7 at the Barker Hangar in Santa Monica. <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 151254, 'screen_type': person}\">Chelsea Handler</a> hosted for the third year in a row, broadcast on E! and streamed on Peacock the following day. <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 974576, 'screen_type': movie}\">Conclave</a> and <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 402431, 'screen_type': movie}\">Wicked</a> led the nominations, with 11 each, and <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 1064213, 'screen_type': movie}\">Anora</a> became the first film in the history of the awards to win Best Picture without winning any other category. The Brazilian film <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 1000837, 'screen_type': movie}\">I'm Still Here</a> was nominated for Best Foreign Language Film.<br/><br/>*<i>Television awards are not included</i>."},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Best Picture","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":1064213,"name":"Anora","image_path":"/v8Pq2MwPXWDCg1MF3UxNlBCkgDA.jpg","director":"Sean Baker","winner":true},{"type":"movie","id":549509,"name":"The Brutalist","image_path":"/52iVP3AtNtpjFiBxlOYCUPXhr47.jpg","director":"Brady Corbet","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":661539,"name":"A Complete Unknown","image_path":"/tXNPJ3XvF4RaEV66Qm9QO3pu3w7.jpg","director":"James Mangold","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":974576,"name":"Conclave","image_path":"/7pMyhSbULMkCCOQCInBYU34Qmf3.jpg","director":"Edward Berger","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":693134,"name":"Dune: Part Two","image_path":"/VMy4UGsI2u3f4fALGeCqCdsQBb.jpg","director":"Denis Villeneuve","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":974950,"name":"Emilia Pérez","image_path":"/8ZOvbX3gCZZatUfaIZFFSAdiboW.jpg","director":"Jacques Audiard","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":1028196,"name"